#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:9
msgid "Learning about actions - tutorial"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:11
msgid ""
"Actions are one of the communication types used for long-duration tasks in a "
"ROS system. This article walks you through using command-line tools to "
"examine and send action goals. A hands-on exercise with Turtlesim helps you "
"understand how goals, feedback, and results work together."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:15
msgid "**Area: Framework | Content-type: tutorial | Experience: beginner**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:19
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:22
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:24
msgid ""
"Actions provide a way to execute long-duration tasks with continuous "
"feedback and the ability to cancel mid-execution. An action client sends a "
"goal to an action server. The action server then acknowledges the goal, "
"streams feedback, and returns a result when done."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:28
msgid ""
"For more information, see :doc:`About actions <../../../About-Actions>`."
msgstr ""

