msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:44
msgid "1 Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:46
msgid ""
"For this tutorial, you need to run two Turtlesim nodes: ``/turtlesim`` and "
"``/teleop_turtle``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:48
msgid "Open a new terminal and run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:50
msgid "$ ros2 run turtlesim turtlesim_node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:54
msgid "Open another terminal and run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:56
msgid "$ ros2 run turtlesim turtle_teleop_key"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:62
msgid "2 Use actions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:64
msgid ""
"When you launch the ``/teleop_turtle`` node, you will see the following "
"message in your terminal:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:66
msgid ""
"Use arrow keys to move the turtle.\n"
"Use G|B|V|C|D|E|R|T keys to rotate to absolute orientations. 'F' to cancel a "
"rotation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:71
msgid ""
"The first line corresponds to the ``cmd_vel`` topic, covered in :doc:"
"`Learning about topics <../../../topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics/"
"Understanding-ROS2-Topics>`. The second line corresponds to an action."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:74
msgid ""
"Notice that the letter keys :kbd:`G`, :kbd:`B`, :kbd:`V`, :kbd:`C`, :kbd:"
"`D`, :kbd:`E`, :kbd:`R`, and :kbd:`T` surround the :kbd:`F` key on a US "
"QWERTY keyboard. Each key's position around :kbd:`F` corresponds to that "
"orientation in Turtlesim. For example, the :kbd:`E` key will rotate the "
"turtle's orientation to the upper left corner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:80
msgid ""
"The figure shows those orientation keys on a QWERTY layout. Teleoperation "
"uses the letters themselves, so if you use a different layout such as "
"Dvorak, press the same letters, even if they do not surround the :kbd:`F` "
"key on your keyboard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:83
msgid ""
"The results are displayed in the terminal where the ``/turtlesim`` node is "
"running. Each time you press one of these keys, you send a goal to an action "
"server that is part of the ``/turtlesim`` node. The goal is to rotate the "
"turtle to face a particular direction. After the turtle completes its "
"rotation, the terminal should display the result:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:88
msgid "[INFO] [turtlesim]: Rotation goal completed successfully"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:92
msgid "The :kbd:`F` key cancels a goal mid-execution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:94
msgid ""
"Try pressing the :kbd:`C` key, and then pressing the :kbd:`F` key before the "
"turtle can complete its rotation. In the terminal where the ``/turtlesim`` "
"node is running, you should see the following message:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:97
msgid "[INFO] [turtlesim]: Rotation goal canceled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:101
msgid ""
"Not only can the client side (your input in the teleoperation node) stop a "
"goal, but the server side (the ``/turtlesim`` node) can as well. When the "
"server side stops processing a goal before the goal is completed, this is "
"known as \"aborting\" the goal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:104
msgid ""
"Press the :kbd:`D` key, then the :kbd:`G` key before the first rotation can "
"complete. In the terminal where the ``/turtlesim`` node is running, you "
"should see the message:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:107
msgid ""
"[WARN] [turtlesim]: Rotation goal received before a previous goal finished. "
"Aborting previous goal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:111
msgid ""
"When a new goal arrives while another is still running, what happens next "
"depends on the action server implementation. ROS does not define a single "
"policy for this case. The goal callback of the server can accept or reject "
"the new goal, and then decides what to do with any goal that is already "
"running. In Turtlesim, the callback accepts the new goal and aborts the "
"previous one, but a different server might reject the new goal, or keep both."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:116
msgid ""
"For more information, see :doc:`About actions <../../../About-Actions>` and "
"the `Actions design article <https://design.ros2.org/articles/actions."
"html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:119
