#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:199
msgid "4 Identify all the actions in the ROS graph"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:201
msgid "To identify all the actions in the ROS graph, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:203
msgid "$ ros2 action list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:209
msgid "/turtle1/rotate_absolute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:213
msgid ""
"This is the only action in the ROS graph right now. ``rotate_absolute`` "
"controls the turtle's rotation. From the ``ros2 node info`` output, there is "
"one action client (part of ``/teleop_turtle``) and one action server (part "
"of ``/turtlesim``) for this action."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:218
msgid "4.1 List all actions and their types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:220
msgid "Like topics and services, actions have types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:222
msgid "To list every active action with its type, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:224
msgid "$ ros2 action list -t"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:230
msgid "/turtle1/rotate_absolute [turtlesim_msgs/action/RotateAbsolute]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:234
msgid ""
"Right now there is only one action, so the list has a single entry. In each "
"line, the action name comes first, followed by the action type in brackets. "
"In this case, ``/turtle1/rotate_absolute`` is the action name and "
"``turtlesim_msgs/action/RotateAbsolute`` is the type. You will use that type "
"later when you send a goal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:240
msgid "5 List the type of an action"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:242
msgid "To check the type of the ``/turtle1/rotate_absolute`` action, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:244
msgid "$ ros2 action type /turtle1/rotate_absolute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:250
msgid "turtlesim_msgs/action/RotateAbsolute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:255
msgid "6 View the details of an action"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:257
msgid "To further introspect the ``/turtle1/rotate_absolute`` action, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:259
msgid "$ ros2 action info /turtle1/rotate_absolute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:265
msgid ""
"Action: /turtle1/rotate_absolute\n"
"Action clients: 1\n"
"    /teleop_turtle\n"
"Action servers: 1\n"
"    /turtlesim"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:273
msgid ""
"This confirms what ``ros2 node info`` showed: the ``/teleop_turtle`` node "
"has an action client and the ``/turtlesim`` node has an action server for "
"the ``/turtle1/rotate_absolute`` action."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:276
msgid "7 View the structure of the action type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:278
msgid ""
"Before sending an action goal, you need to know the structure of the action "
"type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:280
msgid ""
"From the ``ros2 action list -t`` output, the type of ``/turtle1/"
"rotate_absolute`` is ``turtlesim_msgs/action/RotateAbsolute``. To see its "
"structure, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:283
msgid "$ ros2 interface show turtlesim_msgs/action/RotateAbsolute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:287
msgid "The output should look like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:289
msgid ""
"# The desired heading in radians\n"
"float32 theta\n"
"---\n"
"# The angular displacement in radians to the starting position\n"
"float32 delta\n"
"---\n"
"# The remaining rotation in radians\n"
"float32 remaining"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:300
msgid ""
"The section before the first ``---`` is the structure of the goal request. "
"The next section is the structure of the result. The last section is the "
"structure of the feedback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:305
msgid "8 Send an action goal from the command line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:307
msgid "To send an action goal from the command line, use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:309
msgid "$ ros2 action send_goal <action_name> <action_type> <values>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:313
msgid "``<values>`` need to be in YAML format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:315
msgid ""
"The goal field ``theta`` is the desired orientation in radians. The value is "
"absolute, not a relative turn amount. A value of ``1.57`` is about :math:"
"`\\pi/2` radians, so the turtle turns to face roughly a quarter turn from "
"the default rightward orientation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:319
msgid "Keep an eye on the Turtlesim window, then run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:321
msgid ""
"$ ros2 action send_goal /turtle1/rotate_absolute turtlesim_msgs/action/"
"RotateAbsolute \"{theta: 1.57}\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:327
msgid ""
"Waiting for an action server to become available...\n"
"Sending goal:\n"
"   theta: 1.57\n"
"\n"
"Goal accepted with ID: f8db8f44410849eaa93d3feb747dd444\n"
"\n"
"Result:\n"
"  delta: -1.568000316619873\n"
"\n"
"Goal finished with status: SUCCEEDED"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:341
msgid "You should see the turtle rotating."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:343
msgid ""
"All goals have a unique ID, shown in the return message. You can also see "
"the result, a field with the name ``delta``, which is the displacement to "
